## CSS and Token Model

Token CSS is generated from `TypeScript/CSS/tokens.ts`.

| Token file | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `Tokens/colors.css` | Brand and base color variables. |
| `Tokens/typography.css` | Font family, size, line-height, and weight variables. |
| `Tokens/spacing.css` | Spacing scale variables. |
| `Tokens/layout.css` | Container, sidebar, layout gap, and gutter variables. |
| `Tokens/motion.css` | Duration, easing, and transition variables. |
| `Tokens/layer.css` | Layer and z-index variables. |
| `Tokens/breakpoints.css` | Breakpoint variables. |
| `Tokens/surface.css` | Surface, text, border, and notice variables. |
| `Tokens/status.css` | Status and semantic alias variables. |
| `Tokens/effects.css` | Radius, shadow, overlay, transition, animation, and auxiliary effect variables. |

Token category boundaries are explicit: each `TOKEN_FILES` entry in `TypeScript/CSS/tokens.ts` must use the category that matches its output path. Color, typography, spacing, layout, motion, layer, breakpoint, surface, status, and effects categories must not drift across generated token files.

Token family usage discipline is explicit: shared generated CSS must keep using spacing, layout, surface, semantic/status, radius, shadow, motion, and transition token families. Direct color literals are prohibited in `UI/` and `EditorUI/`, and file-local component variables must remain explicitly allowlisted in repository checks.

UI CSS is generated from `TypeScript/CSS/rules.ts`.

`TypeScript/CSS/rules.ts` is the aggregation entrypoint. Rule sources are split by output file unit, such as `rules-components.ts`, `rules-forms.ts`, `rules-content.ts`, and `rules-wysiwyg.ts`, so component families can evolve without turning one source file into the whole system.

| UI file | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `UI/adlaire.css` | Minimal brand color utilities. |
| `UI/base.css` | Reset, base typography, skip links, and base accessibility helpers. |
| `UI/grid.css` | Grid and content container utilities. |
| `UI/layout.css` | Public layout, app shell, split pane, and page structure. |
| `UI/components.css` | Generic UI, Admin UI, Git Provider UI, and reusable components. |
| `UI/site.css` | Site chrome. |
| `UI/forms.css` | Form UI. |
| `UI/content.css` | Content-specific UI. |
| `UI/utilities.css` | Small utilities. |
| `UI/compat-agws.css` | Compatibility layer for the Adlaire-Design CSS contract. |
| `EditorUI/wysiwyg.css` | WYSIWYG Editor UI surface. |

CSS load order for public surfaces is:

`Tokens/colors.css`, `Tokens/typography.css`, `Tokens/spacing.css`, `Tokens/layout.css`, `Tokens/motion.css`, `Tokens/layer.css`, `Tokens/breakpoints.css`, `Tokens/surface.css`, `Tokens/status.css`, `Tokens/effects.css`, then `UI/adlaire.css`, `UI/base.css`, `UI/grid.css`, `UI/layout.css`, `UI/components.css`, `UI/site.css`, `UI/forms.css`, `UI/content.css`, `UI/utilities.css`, `UI/compat-agws.css`.

The CSS target manifest contract keeps `TypeScript/CSS/manifest.ts` `CSS_TARGETS`, generated CSS output files, generated first-line headers, public CSS order, sample loading, and documentation synchronized as one output registry.

The Sample asset/load contract keeps `Samples/design/index.html` aligned with this CSS order, then loads `EditorUI/wysiwyg.css` and `Samples/design/sample.css` after the public CSS contract.

