The JavaScript public surface contract keeps the generated behavior files loadable without bundling: `UI/components.js`, `UI/forms.js`, `UI/content.js`, `EditorUI/editor.js`, and `EditorUI/wysiwyg.js` are loaded by the sample in that order before `Samples/design/sample.js`. Public UI behavior owns delegated document listeners and initialization state, while the structured editor runtime exposes `window.AdlaireEditor`.

